Container packaging excludes lxml's unused isoschematron implementation/resources
because their bundled transformations have unresolved redistribution provenance.
The engine uses lxml HTML/XML parsing, not that optional validator. Third-party
source and notices for distributed native/OS components accompany image review.

The Linux baseline image builds lxml 6.1.3 from its hash-pinned source against
Debian shared libxml2/libxslt libraries. It excludes the upstream wheel statically
bundled GNU libiconv. The image build recipes and exact Debian source/notice
inventory form part of the candidate redistribution dossier.

Runtime images exclude pip/setuptools/wheel and their unused Windows launchers
after installation. Build tools remain only in the non-distributed build stage.

Office import dependencies are retained; unused document-creation templates,
thumbnails and printer metadata are excluded from the Linux baseline image.
PDFMiner's Adobe CMap copyright/license is retained in pdfminer/cmap/README.txt
and collected with the release notices. The final image copies only the reviewed
filesystem so excluded resources cannot remain in preceding image layers.

The Linux image builds NumPy 2.4.6 from hash-pinned source against Debian shared
BLAS/LAPACK and GNU runtimes. It excludes the upstream wheel's vendored numerical
libraries. The exact image notice bundle includes their licenses and matching
corresponding-source references; Python installation extras retain their own
upstream artifact contents and terms.
